# Command palette open-lag receipt, condition 4 of 4: PALETTE OPEN, text
# edits.
#
# Each character is its own step, so each lands on its own frame: `type abc`
# is one step delivering three chars, which would hide per-keystroke cost in a
# single frame.  This block is where `suggestion_runs` and `suggestion_refits`
# earn their place - every edit recomputes the list, and the refit counter says
# how often it was ranked twice for one keystroke.
#
# The typed word is "inspector" because the actions lane matches on lowercased
# SUBSTRING, so every prefix of it still matches "Open Inspector pane". A word
# whose prefixes stop matching would empty the list part-way through and make
# the later keystrokes measure the cheap path while claiming to measure the
# expensive one. The first character is typed and asserted BEFORE the measured
# block for the same reason: a receipt that ranked an empty list would report a
# reassuring number for work nobody does.
#
# MEASURED BLOCK: the 8 typed characters below, 56 frames (each `type` is one
# frame and each `settle 5` is six, the countdown plus the step that sets it),
# followed by one frame for `log`. The harness skips that trailing frame and
# reads the 45 before it.
settle 30
key escape
open mere://alpha
open mere://beta
settle 20
assert visible
omnibar actions
assert omnibar open
type i
settle 20
assert suggestions >= 1
type n
settle 5
type s
settle 5
type p
settle 5
type e
settle 5
type c
settle 5
type t
settle 5
type o
settle 5
type r
settle 5
log palette lag: open text-edit sample complete
